rial in accordance with GCPs or applicable regulatory guidelines, failed inspections of clinical trial<span style="letter-spacing:-0.7pt;"> </span>operations<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>or<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>trial<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>sites<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>by<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>the<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>FDA<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>or<span style="letter-spacing:-0.7pt;"> </span>comparable<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>foreign<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>regulatory<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>authorities,<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>unforeseen<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>safety<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>issues or adverse side effects, failure to establish or achieve clinically meaningful trial endpoints, changes in governmental<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>regulations<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>or<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span>administrative<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>actions<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span>or<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>lack<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span>of<span style="letter-spacing:0.9pt;"> </span>adequate<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span>funding<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>to<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>continue<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span>the<span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;"> </span>clinical<span style="letter-spacing:-0.05pt;"> </span><span style="letter-spacing:-0.1pt;">trial.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Clinical trials frequently are delayed or terminated as a result of<span style="letter-spacing:2pt;"> </span>ambig