pt;"> </span>on<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>a<span style="letter-spacing:-0.65pt;"> </span>timely basis or at all, and there may be risks associated with the acquisition that we did not previously anticipate, such as unanticipated liabilities.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">We<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>also<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>may<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>enter<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>into<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>a<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>variety<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>of<span style="letter-spacing:0.45pt;"> </span>other<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>business<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>arrangements,<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>including<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>strategic<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>collaborations,<span style="letter-spacing:-0.5pt;"> </span>joint ventures, restructurings, divestitures, business combinations and investments. Any future transactions could increase<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>our<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>near<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>and<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>long-term<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>expenditures,<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>result<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>in<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>potentially<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>dilutive<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>issuances<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>of our<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>equity<span style="letter-spacing:-0.25pt;"> </span>securities, including our common stock, or the incurrence of debt, contingent liabilities, amortization expenses or acquired in-process research and development expenses, any of which could affect our business, financial condition, liquidity and results of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Future acquisitions may require us to obtain additional financing, which may not be available on favorable terms or at all. These transactions may never be successful and may require significant time and attention of our management. In addition, the integration of any business or assets may be disruptive, complex, risky and costly and we may never realize the full benefits of<span style="letter-spacing:1.35pt;"> </span>the acquisition.</p></div><div style="clear:both;display:table;margin-bottom:30pt;min-height:27.35pt;width:100%;"><div style="display:table-cell;vertical-align:bottom;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">92</p></div></div></div>
